WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.280
Shark cartilage supplements
are promoted

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.160
by some alternative
medicine practitioners

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.878
due to their supposed
anti-cancer properties.

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:13.800
Is there any truth to that?
Let’s find out.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.696
"The Truth About
Shark Cartilage Pills"

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.720
An assessment of websites on
complementary and alternative medicine

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.880
for cancer found that many
endorse unproven therapies

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.840
and some that are outright dangerous,

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.640
potentially exploiting highly
vulnerable patients

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.760
and enriching irresponsible
snake oil peddlers,

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.040
or for that matter, shark
cartilage peddlers,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.840
accounting for millions of
dollars of sales every year.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.800
Why shark cartilage of all things?

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.640
Interest in shark cartilage
as an anticancer agent arose

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:57.840
because many people believe
that sharks did not get cancer.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:00.400
Why would they think such a thing?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.760
Because some shark cartilage supplement
hawker wrote a book called,

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:06.960
"Sharks Don't Get Cancer."

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:09.600
But that's simply not true.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.840
Sharks do get cancer.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.000
Both benign and cancerous lesions have
been reported in 21 species of sharks

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.120
more than 9 families.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:22.400
For example, this oral tumor spilling
out of the mouth of a great white.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:29.760
Now some shark cartilage distributors insist
instead that sharks just rarely get cancer,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.560
but actual cancer rates in sharks
have never been determined.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.480
There's simply been no
systematic tumor surveys of sharks

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.920
for them to make such a claim.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.240
But look, even if sharks were
less susceptible to cancer,

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.320
how can one logically jump from that
to cancer patients benefiting

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.360
from eating powdered
cartilage from a shark?

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.240
We know, for example, that there
are certain proteins that allow

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.280
some bacteria to survive in
like boiling hot springs.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:02.560
Uh, does that mean if we eat those bacteria
we can survive boiling water, too?

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.800
It doesn't make any sense.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:09.760
The illogic behind the pursuit of shark
cartilage therapies has implications

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:11.680
beyond the reduction of shark populations

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.720
and the misdirection of patients
to ineffective cancer therapies.

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.600
The stuff may be harmful,
and I'm not just talking about

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.040
the rare case of shark
cartilage-induced liver inflammation.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:29.920
Shark products can contain the neurotoxin
BMAA, which I've talked about before.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.360
It's been detected at elevated levels

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:37.200
in the brains of Alzheimer's
disease and ALS patients,

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.480
and may play a role in the development
of neurodegenerative disease.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.480
So like the consumption
of shark fin soup or

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.640
something may pose a significant health risk,

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:49.920
but what about shark cartilage supplements?

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:53.680
They tested sixteen commercial shark
cartilage supplements, right off the shelves,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.360
and found BMAA in fifteen out of sixteen.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.720
But look, even if shark cartilage supplements
carry pro-inflammatory properties,

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.160
which could pose a potential health risk
for consumers, we're talking about cancer.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:12.560
There are chemotherapy agents that
are life-threateningly dangerous,

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.240
but sometimes the benefits can outweigh
the risks when confronted with cancer.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.720
So the question then becomes: are
there any benefits to shark cartilage?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.600
I mean, it's not a completely whacky idea.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.920
Cartilage, in general, is highly resistant
to invasion by tumor cells,

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:36.080
so maybe there's some cartilage-
derived anti-invasion factor?

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.120
Less interesting alternative explanations
are that it's just hard for the cancer

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.480
to penetrate the cartilage, or perhaps
because of the poor blood supply

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.000
in cartilage, cancer doesn't consider
it particularly fertile ground.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:52.880
But maybe that lack of blood vessels
in cartilage can be exploited.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.480
The reason that no blood vessels
end up in cartilage is because

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:59.520
cartilage cells produce
angiogenesis inhibitors,

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:01.440
blood vessel creation inhibitors.

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:07.280
And so maybe we can starve tumor growth
by infusing these cartilage factors.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:12.880
What scientists do is implant
tumors into the eyeballs of rabbits,

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.800
so they can visualize how many blood
vessels the tumor is able to draw to itself.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:21.920
And indeed, shark cartilage contains
inhibitors of tumor angiogenesis.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:26.160
Such findings made the sales
of shark cartilage skyrocket,

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.880
driving two shark species
to the brink of extinction.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.640
But cow cartilage does the same thing.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.200
Here, they used bovine cartilage.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.960
And so does human cartilage,
for that matter.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.840
So why sell shark cartilage?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.720
Well, it does sound so much more exotic,

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.400
and sharks have like 10 times
more cartilage per animal.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.720
One 20-foot shark could net
like 50 pounds of cartilage.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.720
Just because cartilage has blood vessel
inhibiting chemicals in it, though,

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.840
doesn't mean if cancer patients
eat it, it will help them.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:07.440
It's kind of like magical thinking: shark
cartilage stops blood vessel growth,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.600
thus, by consuming shark cartilage,
humans will somehow be protected.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.680
I mean, the shark cartilage protein
molecules would seem to be

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:18.640
too large to be absorbed by the gut.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:22.000
It's not like you're injecting shark cartilage
into your bloodstream through an IV.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:26.560
But there was this rat study
that did find that

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:28.560
just feeding shark cartilage to the animals,

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:30.960
you could cut down on blood vessel
growth within their bodies.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:36.320
OK, but does that translate out to stopping
the growth and spread of cancer?

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:40.880
Apparently not, as none of the
shark cartilage doses tested

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:46.160
had any retarding effect on cancer
growth or spread in tumor-bearing mice,

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:52.240
but just because it doesn't work in rodents
doesn't mean it doesn't work in humans.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.000
To find that out you need
to put it to the test,

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:03.765
evaluating shark cartilage in human
cancer patients, which we'll cover next.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:10.240
When it comes to marketing
unproven cancer treatments,

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.040
the Internet has become the Wild West.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.960
Fraudsters are able to take advantage
of people like never before.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:23.680
"Cancer Patients Find Quackery on The Web,"
bemoaned the National Cancer Institute.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.760
Did you know there were more
than 200,000 documents

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.280
about cancer on the web?

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:36.080
What? When was this published?
Oh, 1996.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.320
That's just a few years
after the web was born.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.680
Not to worry, though, said the author of
Dr. Linden's Guide to Online Medicine.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.360
It takes a lot of time and money
to maintain a Web page.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:52.640
So don't worry, the mass of information
on the Internet will dwindle

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:56.000
during the next few years
as the Internet matures.

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:04.640
Right! Yes, dwindling from 200,000
down to a mere quarter of a billion.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.000
And one the most commonly recommended
"alternative cancer cures"

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.200
on popular websites is shark cartilage.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:20.000
Much has been made in recent years of
the mystical aura afforded to the stuff.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:24.320
Clearly part of it is the visceral fear of
cancer, combined with a healthy respect

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:27.760
for a creature that's survived basically
unchanged since prehistoric times.

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:30.720
It has been reported that
sharks rarely get cancer,

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:33.120
and their skeleton is
made out of cartilage,

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:35.680
and so logic has led some to believe

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.320
that this must be the reason
for sharks' relative health.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.800
Not exactly sure that's logical,
but they do have a lot of cartilage.

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.720
Cartilage, in general, has few blood vessels,

00:07:46.720 --> 00:07:48.800
and blood vessels are
important for cancer growth,

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:54.320
and all this conspired to prime fraught
cancer patients for shameful exploitation

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.120
by pseudoscience and
the supplement industry

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:01.840
with the addition of just one myth,
and that's sharks don't get cancer.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.480
But they do get cancer, after all.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:09.120
Just another layer of fallacious arguments,

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:13.360
successfully convincing desperate cancer
patients to buy ineffective products.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:19.680
But wait, you don't know if it's
ineffective until you put it to the test.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:25.200
Sixty patients with a variety of advanced
cancers, given like a dozen scoops a day

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:31.200
of shark cartilage, and not
a single, even partial, response

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.760
was noted in any of their tumors.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:38.000
Ineffective with no salutary
effect on the quality of life.

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:42.400
In fact, suffering significant
gastrointestinal toxicity from the stuff,

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.680
all the while the tumors
progressed in all the patients.

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.440
But what's missing from this survival graph?

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.000
What happened in the control group?

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:55.360
There was no control group.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:58.640
So while this is what you'd expect
to see in advanced cancer patients,

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:02.560
how do we know the cancers wouldn't
have progressed even faster

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:04.400
without the shark cartilage?

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:07.200
That's why we need
randomized controlled trials,

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.320
but there weren't any until
the Mayo clinic stepped up.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:15.040
A randomized, placebo-controlled,
double-blind, clinical trial

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:18.640
for patients with incurable breast
or colorectal carcinoma.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:23.120
Data on a total of 83 patients were analyzed,

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:29.920
and there was no difference in survival
between patients getting shark cartilage

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:35.840
versus those getting placebo, nor any
suggestion of improvement in quality of life.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.440
There was evidently
a prostate cancer study, too.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.480
Only 5 patients were even
able to complete the study,

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.880
and in all five their cancers
continued to progress unabated.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.880
So unfortunately, the claims for
the benefits of shark cartilage

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:53.520
are completely unsubstantiated

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:57.440
by any objective data
from controlled clinical trials.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.280
Not so fast, said
supplement manufacturers.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.080
Maybe these crude commercial
shark cartilage powders just

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.360
don't have high enough levels of whatever
active components there may be,

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:13.680
so cancer patients should instead be
taking shark cartilage extract pills.

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.280
So the National Cancer Institute said fine,

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.760
we'll test that, too, just
to make absolutely sure.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:23.520
And so they funded a randomized,
double-blinded, placebo-controlled trial

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:25.360
to put it to the test.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.120
Unlike the other shark cartilage
dietary supplement studies,

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:35.440
they used the purified extract, and
the study outcome was unambiguous.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:37.200
It failed.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.640
The shark cartilage group lived 14 months,
and the placebo group lived 15 months.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:45.200
So no significant difference in survival

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.160
or to time to progression
or tumor response rate.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.960
So these clinical studies suggest

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:54.160
shark cartilage is not just
an unproven cancer remedy,

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:56.720
but actually a well disproven one.

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:01.280
Yet despite the overwhelming evidence
to the contrary such claims persisted.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:06.880
For example, the huckster who started it all
wrote a sequel, "Sharks Still Don't Get Cancer."

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.400
Perhaps the only cure for this
myth is to spread the rumor

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:14.560
that cartilage from the noses of
such quacks fights cancer, too.

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:19.120
Anyway, if you really wanted
to eat angiogenesis inhibitors,

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.360
why sit down to a bowl
of cartilage powder,

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:28.240
when you could just eat an apple, or drink
green tea, or turmeric, or pomegranate,

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:30.560
berries and nuts, soybeans,
flaxseeds, broccoli---

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:36.853
all of which have been shown
to have anti-angiogenic effects.

